Negative control for `featureAcTags` (the `@todo` exclusion).

Points the `@todo` marker at a spelling no feature uses, so a scenario tagged
`@todo` is reported as a live AC. The AC link then demands a proving spec for a
capability deliberately parked, and the only way back to green is to write a
test for something nobody built.

The assertion that must go RED: the one asserting `featureAcTags` omits the AC
id of a `@todo`-tagged scenario.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

